Package: wgtcp-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         dkms,
         build-essential,
         libmnl-dev,
         pkg-config
Recommends: wireguard-tools
Description: WireGuard-over-TCP (WGTCP) module + wg tool, DKMS source
 WGTCP adds a TCP carrier to WireGuard (in addition to the standard UDP
 transport) for networks where UDP is blocked. This is a DKMS source
 package: it ships the patched WireGuard module source and builds it
 per-host, per-kernel at install time (and auto-rebuilds on kernel
 upgrade). The built module is named wireguard and installs into
 updates/dkms/, overriding the in-tree module via depmod precedence
 (reversible: dkms remove restores stock). The modified wg userspace tool
 (transport selector) is compiled on the host and installed to
 /usr/local/bin/wg.
 .
 Architecture: all because the package carries source, not binaries; each
 host compiles natively for its own kernel and architecture.
 .
 Single portable source: builds on Linux 6.12 through 7.2 via
 LINUX_VERSION_CODE guards.
